# Spec-driven workflow

## Before coding

1. Name the feature spec file:
   - Investing: `docs/mvp/features/<feature>.md` (e.g. `cheap-stocks.md`)
   - Credit: under `credit/docs/` (e.g. `credit/docs/features/css-chapter5-mart-and-scoring.md`)
2. Read domain constraints:
   - Investing: `docs/mvp/architecture/architecture.md` (frozen historical vision; point-in-time data, exclusions, MLflow, paper trading, universe rules)
   - Credit: `credit/CONTEXT.md` + `CONTEXT-MAP.md` (+ the feature spec)
3. If scope is unclear, ask the user and record the answer in the spec (open questions or decisions tables).

## During work

- Do not add features without a corresponding feature document under the matching domain tree. Create or extend the spec first.
- Keep changes aligned with that domain’s scope and any “Out of scope” sections in the spec.
- Do not mix investing and credit domain language (see `CONTEXT-MAP.md`).

## After implementation

Update the same feature spec:

- **Implementation status** (planned | in progress | done)
- Closed decisions and acceptance criteria
- Links to modules or paths when code exists

## No orphan work

If the user requests code without a spec, propose the spec outline first or draft the minimal spec section needed, then implement.
